MediaTek MET_CORE (met_drv) - vendored in-tree for built-in linking
====================================================================

These sources are the MediaTek MET (Mobile Enhancement Technology) driver
core, version MET_BACKEND_VERSION "6.2.0", vendored into the kernel tree so
the MET broker (../met_api.c) and the real driver core link into the same
vmlinux via CONFIG_MTK_MET_BUILT_IN.

Provenance
----------
  Upstream repository : https://github.com/rabbit-hmi-oss/android_kernel_modules_rabbit_mt6765
  Pinned commit       : 0afdf059a0dfa17becc4bbe47363280a42224c2f
  Upstream path       : met_drv/4.14
  License             : GPL-2.0 (per-file "GNU General Public License version 2")
  Local mirror        : kernel/evergo-sukisu-susfs-nomount/src/mt6833-met-modules/met_drv/4.14

Only the mt6833 platform directory, the "common" core and the platform
feature descriptor are vendored. Build artifacts (*.o, .*.cmd, *.d,
*.symversions), the vendor "default" fallback stub core (never reachable:
a missing platform directory is a hard build error here) and the mt6739/
mt6768/mt6781/mt6785/mt6853/mt6873/mt6877/mt6885/mt6893 platform
directories were not copied.

Vendored layout
---------------
  met_core/common/            MET core (sampler, tag, EMI, GPU, thermal, ...)
  met_core/common/emi/...     EMI bandwidth monitors (SEDA3_5 selected)
  met_core/common/sspm/...    on-die MET SSPM backend
  met_core/common/tinysys/v1/ tinysys (SSPM + MCUPM) logging backends
  met_core/mt6833/            platform feature descriptor + register data

Platform selection
------------------
The everpal device is MT6833 while CONFIG_MTK_PLATFORM names the mt6853
driver family. The parent Makefile therefore overrides MTK_PLATFORM to
mt6833 from CONFIG_MACH_MT6833, matching the vendor Makefile. Because this
tree ships only met_core/mt6833, a missing platform directory is a hard
build error instead of a silent fallback, so a wrong/partial feature set
cannot be selected.

Local changes relative to the pinned upstream commit
----------------------------------------------------
1. common/Kbuild: "obj-y := met.o" -> "obj-y += met.o" in the built-in
   branch so met_api.o (added to obj-y by ../Makefile) is not dropped.
   "MET_CORE := common" -> "MET_CORE ?= common" so the in-tree build can set
   the met_core/-prefixed object paths.
2. Added "(void)" prototypes to 12 K&R-style empty-parameter definitions
   rejected by clang -Werror=strict-prototypes (kernel Makefile:1004):
     common/emi/SEDA3_5/mtk_emi_bm.c: MET_GET_DRAM_TYPE()
     common/tinysys/v1/mcupm/mcupm_met_ipi_handle.c: start/stop_mcupm_ipi_recv_thread()
     common/tinysys/v1/sspm/sspm_met_ipi_handle.c: start/stop_sspm_ipi_recv_thread()
     common/tinysys/v1/tinysys_mgr.c: ondiemet_log_manager_start/stop,
         ondiemet_start/stop/extract, _remove_mcupm_node
     common/v7_pmu_hw.c: armv7_pmu_disable_cyc_intr()  (arm-only build path)
3. Header search order: the kernel's drivers/misc/mediatek/include/mt-plat/
   met_drv.h shares the MET_DRV include guard with common/met_drv.h. In a
   full Image build the kernel copy was resolved first for metk_emi_bm.h and
   friends, hiding the donor's MET_TRACE. ../Makefile now prepends this
   directory to LINUXINCLUDE so the vendor header wins; no source change.
4. Renamed the MET-local tracing_mark_write() helper to
   met_tracing_mark_write() (definition in common/met_tag_ex.c, extern in
   common/met_tag.h, callers in common/sampler.c). The unrelated global
   tracing_mark_write(const char *) in drivers/mailbox/mtk-cmdq-mailbox.c
   would otherwise be a duplicate vmlinux symbol once MET_CORE is built-in
   instead of a separate met.ko.

No functional behavior was changed by these edits.
